(7046676, 1071337, 100393, '<td valign="top"><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1051747" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/100000-104999/100393/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1051747.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/100000-104999/100393/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1051747.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/100000-104999/100393/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1051747.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>Awarded for the May 2013 Free Study, for the reasons identified below. <br/> <br/>This image has caused me to stop and pay attention. That means it is in my 7-10 voting band. (Voted earlier).<br/> <br/>Additionally, it is highly interesting/eclectic meaning it keeps me here long enough to offer a longer comment and a vote of 8 or more. <br/> <br/>This is my only 10 this month - I like it very much. Furthermore I think it enriches the DPC collective portfolio. Put simply, I wish we saw more stuff like this. Let me tell you why it pushes all the right buttons for me: <br/> <br/>1. What a fantastic POV - eclectic and effective.<br/> <br/>2. Brilliant exposure in difficult conditions, excellent shadow detail without compromising the contrast.<br/> <br/>3. That eye- captivating yet aloof!<br/> <br/>4. The overall composition with the dog looming from the top right corner of the image.<br/> <br/>5. That band of cloud, I love the way in transects the image.<br/> <br/>Brilliant stuff.</td>', '  Awarded for the May 2013 Free Study, for the reasons identified below.  This image has caused me to stop and pay attention. That means it is in my 7-10 voting band. (Voted earlier). Additionally, it is highly interesting/eclectic meaning it keeps me here long enough to offer a longer comment and a vote of 8 or more.  This is my only 10 this month - I like it very much. Furthermore I think it enriches the DPC collective portfolio. Put simply, I wish we saw more stuff like this. Let me tell you why it pushes all the right buttons for me:  1. What a fantastic POV - eclectic and effective. 2. Brilliant exposure in difficult conditions, excellent shadow detail without compromising the contrast. 3. That eye- captivating yet aloof! 4. The overall composition with the dog looming from the top right corner of the image. 5. That band of cloud, I love the way in transects the image. Brilliant stuff.', '2013-06-02 15:54:49.000000', NULL, 1),
